This is a CBP ruling on a power reclining sectional sofa with a wooden frame. Upholstered seats with a wooden frame fall under heading 9401.61 (other seats, with wooden frames, upholstered). Parts of seats go to 9401.90, but the pieces here are incomplete seating sections that CBP typically classifies as seats.

Reclining seats with a wooden frame might fall under 9401.61.40 (upholstered, with wooden frame, other than of a kind used for motor vehicles, other, nonconvertible to beds). The 9401.61 subheadings are: 9401.61.20 (seats of a kind used for aircraft, probably under 9401.10/20), 9401.61.30 (Theater seats?), 9401.61.40 (Other: Convertible into beds, other than...), 9401.61.60 (Other). The statistical suffixes: 9401.61.4011 is "Other: Seats of a kind used for... Household: convertible"? Based on memory, 9401.61.40 covers "Other: Nonconvertible to beds" in the group "Upholstered," with 9401.61.4011 as "Motion-picture theater seats?" That is uncertain. I recall 9401.61.6011 as "Other: Upholstered: Other: Other" and 9401.61.6031 as "Other." In recent rulings for sectional sofas, CBP classified them in 9401.61.4011 (upholstered, wooden frame, nonconvertible to beds, "Stationary") or 9401.61.4031. The commonly cited code for upholstered wooden-frame seats, other, is 9401.61.4011 and for reclining sofas I believe it's 9401.61.4011 as well.

{"hts_code": "9401.61.4011", "reason": "The upholstered seating sections with wooden frames are not convertible to beds and are classified as other upholstered seats with wooden frames in heading 9401, subheading 9401.61."}
